{"id":"atlas-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3600,"height":200,"text":"**Power and battery / NOS · 1.43-B**\n\n23 system members · 20 one-hop ghost neighbours · 48 canonical edges\nEvery incoming and outgoing edge of a member is shown, including parallel edges. Ghost cards retain status text and gap badges; grey borders mark neighbours unless a high/critical gap requires red. Arrows retain source direction; MISSING means an absent connection, not working data flow.\nCyan data · orange control · green persist · purple schedule · yellow UI · red event.\n[[NOS System Map.canvas|Return to overview]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"hw-battery-adc","type":"text","x":2556,"y":396,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Battery ADC (GPIO4, divider 3)**\nMeasures the system rail on GPIO4 (ADC1 ch3,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Sampled once a second by the battery sampler.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"3"},
{"id":"hw-button","type":"text","x":3012,"y":396,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**BOOT button (GPIO0)**\nSide button on GPIO0. ISR with 25 ms…\n\nruns: ISR on edge. Works in every display state.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-co5300-panel","type":"text","x":3468,"y":396,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)**\n466x466 RGB565 AMOLED on QSPI (CS9, CLK10,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Driven by the flush task; DISPOFF/SLPIN in sleep states.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"hw-deep-sleep","type":"text","x":3924,"y":396,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Deep sleep (ext0 GPIO0 wake)**\nLowest power state, entered only by the…\n\nruns: Only on explicit POWER OFF.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"drv-hal-esp32","type":"text","x":2328,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**HAL glue (hal_esp32.c)**\nImplements the core/hal.h contract on ESP-…\n\nruns: Library code called from every task.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"drv-battery","type":"text","x":2784,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Battery sampler and percent model**\n8 ADC reads per second, median, EMA 1/5,…\n\nruns: Triggered at 1 Hz from board-sense, screen on or off.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"3"},
{"id":"drv-ext-hal","type":"text","x":3240,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Strap HAL contract and presence mask**\nhal_ext_* contract shared by all strap…\n\nruns: Serviced by the ext task, wakes at most every 50 ms.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"drv-sleep-protocol","type":"text","x":3696,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Sleep park protocol**\nAt shutdown the board asks each strap module…\n\nruns: Shutdown path only.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"3"},
{"id":"drv-batt-log","type":"text","x":4152,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**BLE battery history ring**\nhal_batt_log_tick fills a 1440-entry mV ring…\n\nruns: Never runs.\n\n`DEAD-CODE`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"task-board-sense","type":"text","x":2556,"y":1876,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**board-sense task**\nIMU loop (3 reads per cycle, about 150/s)…\n\nruns: prio 2, 4 KB static, no affinity. 20 ms cycle, always on, screen off included.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"1"},
{"id":"task-ui","type":"text","x":3012,"y":1876,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**main / app_main UI loop**\nBoot, power-state machine, serial command…\n\nruns: core 0, prio 1, 8192 B. ON about 60 Hz (40 Hz authored); AOD/SENSOR 1 Hz frames; OFF 50 Hz loop, no frames.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"task-touch","type":"text","x":3468,"y":1876,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**touch task**\nPolls the FT3168 and pushes points into a…\n\nruns: core 1, prio 5. 10 ms ON, 40 ms (25 Hz) otherwise; keeps polling screen-off.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"task-board-fs","type":"text","x":3924,"y":1876,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**board-fs task**\nDevice retry, SD mount retry, pedometer NVS…\n\nruns: prio 1, 4 KB. 100 ms loop, always on.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|1 gap]]\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"eng-input","type":"text","x":2784,"y":2640,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Input recogniser and router**\nTurns touch points and button edges into…\n\nruns: UI task, every frame.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"eng-power-states","type":"text","x":3240,"y":2640,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF**\nState machine in the UI loop. ON renders;…\n\nruns: UI task loop, every pass (20 ms delay when not ON).\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"eng-pm-dfs","type":"text","x":3696,"y":2640,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**DFS / PM locks (80-240 MHz)**\nesp_pm: the UI loop holds an nos-ui lock per…\n\nruns: UI task, around each loop iteration.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"svc-phone-link","type":"text","x":48,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Phone line pump and status reporter**\nphone_tick: drains NUS lines, tracks…\n\nruns: svc_tick on the UI task.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|14 gaps]]\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"svc-track","type":"text","x":504,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**GPS track recorder**\nSamples GNSS fixes into a 4096-point PSRAM…\n\nruns: svc_tick; keeps recording with Navigate closed.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps]]\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"1"},
{"id":"svc-wake","type":"text","x":960,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Wake service (config, learn, tick)**\nRaise-to-wake configuration (wake_cfg),…\n\nruns: UI task every pass (about 50 Hz) when display not ON.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"3"},
{"id":"svc-cmd-exec","type":"text","x":1416,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**USB command dispatcher (cmd_exec)**\nExecutes about 130 text verbs and the req…\n\nruns: UI task, drained each loop pass.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"svc-sports-logger","type":"text","x":1872,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Sports journal (sensor/event logger)**\nQueues 64 B checksummed records (SP_IMU,…\n\nruns: sports_tick 1 Hz; 60 s records; IMU records from board-sense.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"svc-knock","type":"text","x":2328,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Double-knock detector**\nDetects knocks from raw accel and gyro at…\n\nruns: board-sense per sample.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"svc-system","type":"text","x":2784,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**System status service (svc_sys)**\nMirrors battery percent/charging/rail, phone…\n\nruns: sys_tick 1 Hz.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"3"},
{"id":"svc-power-policy","type":"text","x":3240,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Power policy**\nDecides the idle target (SENSOR by default,…\n\nruns: UI task each loop pass.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"3"},
{"id":"svc-ringer","type":"text","x":3696,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Ringer and ring-screen manager**\nPriority arbiter find > call > alarm >…\n\nruns: svc_tick.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Services hub|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"svc-workout","type":"text","x":4152,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Workout session engine**\nRuns sessions (start/pause/lap/finish),…\n\nruns: workout_tick in svc_tick; 1 Hz screen off; checkpoint 30 s.\n\n`PARTIAL` · ⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"1"},
{"id":"svc-background-jobs","type":"text","x":4608,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Background jobs monitor**\nTracks 13 job states (motion, steps, calorie…\n\nruns: background_tick, internally 1 Hz.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"svc-prefs","type":"text","x":5064,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Preferences service (nos_prefs)**\nOwns the 52 B nos_prefs struct, defaults,…\n\nruns: prefs_tick on the UI task, only when the persistence window is open.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"svc-motion-wake","type":"text","x":5520,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Raise-to-wake detector**\nPickup/turn gesture detector fed by the 3…\n\nruns: Per sample from wake service.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
